<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-14.webp"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-14.webp" alt="" width="498" height="498" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-114155" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-14.webp 498w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-14-300x300.webp 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-07-14-150x150.webp 150w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 498px) 100vw, 498px" /></a></p>
<p><a href="https://debbugs.gnu.org/cgi/bugreport.cgi?bug=66390">&#8220;There&#8217;s only madness down that road.&#8221;</a></p>
<p>My solution to the <tt>url.el</tt> parts of <a href="https://emacsninja.com/posts/cve-2025-1244-from-emacs-url-handler-to-rce.html" data-cached-time="2025-07-14T06:49:51" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/cache-2025-07-14-web.webp" onmouseenter="hoverLink(event)">Vasilij Schneidermann excellent writeup</a> would, as always, be:</p>
<pre>diff --git a/lisp/url/url.el b/lisp/url/url.el
index b4ece5faeb..8ea491efb0 100644
--- a/lisp/url/url.el
+++ b/lisp/url/url.el
@@ -191,7 +191,8 @@ url-retrieve-internal
       (setq url (url-generic-parse-url url)))
   (if (not (functionp callback))
       (error "Must provide a callback function to url-retrieve"))
-  (unless (url-type url)
+  (when (or (not (url-type url))
+            (not (member (url-type url) '("http" "https" "file"))))
     (error "Bad url: %s" (url-recreate-url url)))
   (setf (url-silent url) silent)
   (setf (url-asynchronous url) url-asynchronous)
</pre>
<p>(Along with making redirects saner, of course.)</p>
